# Paul Trap Analysis Components

## Electrode
The [Electrode](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Electrode.py) class contains information about the electrical potential of individual electrodes and uses xarray to store the potential data with 3D grid points. Key features:
- Supports 3D potential data
- Uses xarray for data organization
- Handles potential interpolation

## Trap
The [Trap](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Trap.py) class combines electrodes and trap parameters. It consists of:
- Dictionary of Electrodes in the trap
- Dictionary of basic trap parameters (mass, charge, drive frequency, etc.)
- Uses pandas dataframe for user-friendly queries

## Multipoles
The [Multipoles](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Multipoles.py) class expands the trapping potential in multipoles (spherical harmonic basis). It allows finding efficient electrode voltage solutions to generate specific potential shapes.

## Particle
The [Particle](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Particle.py) class represents particles trapped within the Paul trap, including properties such as mass, charge, and position.

## Trajectory
The [Trajectory](mdc:PaulTrapAnalysis/components/Trajectory.py) class enables analysis of particle trajectories within the trap, helping understand stability and confinement properties.
